{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/686066-my-first-story-advice","id":686066,"title":"My first story. Advice?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-02T13:01:06-07:00","id":686066,"title":"My first story. Advice?","content":"So I'm writing my first story and thinking of it as a sort of tutorial and introduction for the players and I. It starts with our players as newly sired vampires at a Carthian run concert. However several representatives from other covenants are their for varying reasons but ultimately they are each there to recruit these new vampires to their cause. Also the main hook is the search for a rumored powerful artifact each covenant is interested in acquiring. Any tips or comments? Is this a realistic idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8152-xizzicks","name":"Xizzicks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T13:05:23-07:00","id":686093,"title":"","content":"That seems fine. One important thing you'll want to look out for is that the recruiters probably aren't going to be begging, they'd come at the player characters acting as if they were doing them a favor by possibly allowing them to join their elite club.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T13:44:45-07:00","id":686134,"title":"","content":"Take some time to look over the players' Aspriations and figure out what common ground they might have between them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T15:39:01-07:00","id":686212,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind covenants don't share their secrets easily so recruiters will withhold some information about what their covenant does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T19:30:48-07:00","id":686336,"title":"","content":"Starting in a &quot;safe&quot; social situation and introducing the various factions is a good start.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1459/Vampire-The-Requiem-Demo-Full\" target=\"_blank\">The free demo for Vampire: The Requiem first edition</a> starts with newly Embraced vampires being introduced to the local court before leading in to a longer adventure. It could be a very useful source of ideas, even if you don't use the plot directly.<br /> <br /> The Second Edition free quickstart <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114063/Reap-the-Whirlwind\" target=\"_blank\">Reap The Whirlwind</a> has a very different introductory adventure, where the PCs get a chance to kill an unpopular Prince and then find out why nobody else had done so. While less directly applicable, it still features an example court with various special interests and secrets, and an item some of them will go looking for.<br /> <br /> (The first and second edition <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> rulebooks also have an adventure (not available separately) called &quot;Baptism by Fire&quot; in which new Kindred in a small city encounter representatives of various factions and interests.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T20:54:10-07:00","id":686445,"title":"","content":"Thanks everybody! Could I tell my players in character through email about their surroundings and how to interact with them. Receive responses and roll any needed die etc, ST stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8152-xizzicks","name":"Xizzicks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T07:57:56-07:00","id":696088,"title":"","content":"Well, if you are doing something of an introduction and tutorial to your players with this game, i would suggest waiting out a little before going into the intrigue. Let them &quot;tour&quot; the bloodsucker nightlife a little first. Feeding, hunting, sleep, frenzy and etc, play with the basics first, to help them familiarizing them (and yourself) with the systems and their application - roleplaying through their Requiem and how they experience the changes from human being to the undead predator they now are can be pretty good and intense too.<br /> <br /> How does the embrace shapes her? Does the Favored Attribute dot go (thinking 1st edition here, because i'm not all that familiar with 2nd yet)? What about her 3 discipline dots? A neonate with all clan disciplines at 1 can feel very different from one with Majesty 3 or another with Celerity 1 &amp; Vigor 2 or vice-versa, what can have a strong effect in how a young Daeva (or Gangrel or Mekhet, just change the disciplines in the example) <b>experiences </b>and <b>feels </b>the first nights of her Requiem, and that without going into out-of-clan disciplines territory (uncommon but possible, specially if one's sire was a diablerist or into weird stuff) yet, that can open room for a whole breadth of stuff - just think of Lestat almost entranced with his enhanced senses after becoming a vampire, for one simple but iconic image. The favored attribute, depending on how well it &quot;sinergizes&quot; with her disciplines and previous stats can or not further enhance this feeling of a change/empowerment/growth in a young lick - and let's be honest any discipline at 3 can be quite a ridiculously impressive thing and incredibly dramatic change on itself.<br /> <br /> But not everything is flowers and power trips, so also there's the matter of adaptation to the restrictions and requirements of one's new condition. Some things that i guess can apply to each and every one of the characters to at least some level:<br /> <br /> - Does she live by herself or with friends, lovers or relatives, familiar people who might notice (and look askance at) a sudden change of habits (like not breathing - that can be a <b>very </b>bothersome telltale if one shares the room or bed with another person)? How does one deal with it, getting a new home, awing/dominating/scaring/ghouling them into compliance or telling the truth and hope for the best? Also is that home in some older kindred's domain? What kind of vampire is that figure and how will it react to one or more newbies in its turf?<br /> <br /> - Does one have a job or regular source of income? How does the nocturnal condition impact (or not) in one's lifestyle, study or work? Can these new capacities help in solving any issues, or not? Would one <b>care</b> to continue studying or working after becoming a vampire?<br /> <br /> - The first draught of blood probably comes from one's sire at the embrace (supposing it doesn't have a handy unconscious victim close by to &quot;properly wean her out&quot;) but what about after that? Unless one finds a convenient nearby slaughterhouse or develops Animalism quickly, animal blood will be mostly inacessible due to kindred nature scaring most of them, making it a &quot;too much work for too little good&quot; situation when compared to the (comparatively) easier and far more satisfying temptation of engorging oneself into mortal blood. The longer it takes one to feed again, the greater the chance of losing control due to starvation at a wrong moment and attacking someone one would prefer not to or going too far with a feeding.<br /> <br /> - How many nights before one's first lone hunt? Will it be brutal &amp; savage or deliberate &amp; seductive? Will hunger or inexperience interfere? What if one gets sloppy, or accidentally comes across a hunter, another kindred - or just some random creep or weirdo in the process? Note this may serve to set up an accidental first encounter other local kindred or the Sheriff or his agents (hounds, his ghouls, the hounds own ghouls, etc), either as backstory or actively in game. Also, Blood Sympathy, brood relatives and occasional glimpses of their most emotionally charged moments can always make one's unlife a little random, weird and interesting.<br /> <br /> Overall i would say, explore the basics - learning what powers works for her and what needs, urges &amp; weakness her vampiric self possesses (does one have a normal reflection, blurry or none? Vampires are generated only by embrace or accidental making of revenants is possible?) can be used as the basis for a number of situations, tense, tragic or humorous, with what fits each definition depending on circunstances...<br /> <br /> An armed thug trying to rob you when a loved one is nearby can be tense or tragic but one trying to rob a hungry vampire just out her (failed) first hunt would be quite (darkly) humorous indeed. One memorable example with my players was when one of them, just out of a popular nightclub, was badly run over by a drunk driver in a busy street in front of the place and the poor PC, to avoid breaching the masquerade pretty badly, had to play dead until the ambulance came up and people put it in a black bag, (from where it called by cellphone for help in getting out of the hospital's morgue). They had to some quick thinking to keep this crap on the hush-hush but really enjoyed the whole mess and its colaterals. And yes, i'm a bastard when i feel like it. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Also, who made them into kindred - are their sires bigwigs, nobodies, criminals, passing nomads or something in between? Do they serve as mentor/guide figures, were destroyed or simply watching out from a distance as distant parent/stalker figures? What factions, loyalties and rivalries might they possess? How truly experienced are they and what were their motives? Being the childe or pupil picked by an established elder that has seen the rule of 3 princes and has a decades-long interest in your family will be quite different from being embraced after the frenzied attack of a friend, relative or lover that disappeared (or died) weeks ago (or just yesterday) and can considerably influence their relationship.<br /> <br /> Now speaking of the MacGuffin - why do the covenants want it, or more importantly, why do the want the PCs to collect it for them specifically?<br /> <br /> Why not send some people already of the covenant or have they already done so and are feeling short of manpower (because either their own trackers disappeared, or there's just too many places to look out for)?<br /> <br /> Is it really important for any of the covenants, just a test of what neonates are capable of or a bit of both?<br /> <br /> Are the covenants interested in them because they believe (mistakenly or not) that one or more of them would have an edge over most kindred already after it (Auspex 3+, good contacts in some area relevant to the search, a blood tie with whoever stole/was last seen with the MacGuffin, etc)?<br /> <br /> Sketching out what is its value actual for each group (do they need it, want to destroy it as a threat/abomination/offense or to use it as a negotiation tool with another covenant/faction?) - and how it might react to someone catching it first should be quite invaluable when you do get them into this &quot;fetch quest&quot;.<br /> Also, would any unaligned kindred have an interest of their own in the whole issue?<br /> <br /> Those are my thoughts and opinions overall, hope some of this stuff helps out with you setting up the game. Have fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-10-2015, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T16:34:37-07:00","id":696614,"title":"","content":"If the recruiters are trying to force the newbies into their ranks, I would suggest that they <b>subtly</b> ask them to perform an errand or task that, while it may not overtly combat their rival covenant, may still leave them with a bad first impression. That way, they're already looked upon with suspicion and guilt, thereby making allegiance to the other faction seem like the easiest method by default. Should also be important to note that the newbies don't know who they're pissing off until the mission is almost complete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T04:07:16-07:00","id":696918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/686066-my-first-story-advice?p=696614#post696614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the recruiters are trying to force the newbies into their ranks, I would suggest that they <b>subtly</b> ask them to perform an errand or task that, while it may not overtly combat their rival covenant, may still leave them with a bad first impression. That way, they're already looked upon with suspicion and guilt, thereby making allegiance to the other faction seem like the easiest method by default. Should also be important to note that the newbies don't know who they're pissing off until the mission is almost complete.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, some kindred might do something like that too, though it can backfire on the neonates gaining a dislike of them due to being tricked in messing with other people for them and some might try to go to that other side exactly to make amends or flout them. But then getting the PCs into messes and the unpredictable madness they bring in dealing with them is half the fun, no? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}